Z||000003||Haze_Performance||11-07-2001||04:34 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BlackStang95:<BR><B>My gut instinct is it fits fine, but tire guys usually know what they're talking about?  If none of the gurus get to your question i sugget you follow his advice.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>The reason I doubt them is because, he thinks theres a difference in the 85 Coupe & 85 GT..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> I know thats not the case. Hes tring to sell me a ULTRA HIGH PERFORMANCE tire & I don't want one. I'm looking for ALL SEASON... Thanks for the input BlackStang95.. I feel that they should fit also...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> (I hope)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P><BR>ANYONE ELSE KNOW ?????<P>------------------------------------||||reg||14
Z||000004||Bazooka||11-07-2001||06:53 PM||||Haze,<BR>   I've had a 16x7 1/2" mag on my GT for a couple of years now. The tire size is 2.25/50-16's. There is no interference until you turn the front wheels all the way to the end stop to the left and then there is a slight rub. This is with a 35mm (positive) offset.<BR>*****************************<BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Haze_Performance:So I'm at work & bored.. I called a tire shop & ordered a set of wheels & tires for winter. I wanted 16x7" wheels (40mm offset) & 225/50/16 rubber. They say the tires wont fit the Fiero without problems.. (I'm useing Eibach lowering springs) Now I know Oreif has a set of 15x7" with 225/50/15's on his car & has no problems. Won't the 16"ers work the same? It only makes the wheel a half an inch taller... PLEASE give your input.. I need to call the guy back today..<BR><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>****************************<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Philphine||11-07-2001||10:00 PM||||same size wheels and tires as bazooka for a few years and no problems. i do notice a shiney spot on my a arm but i never feel or hear it rub. it must only happen on a full to the locks turn. i may even try 235/50-16 on front 'cause i have some already.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Haze_Performance||11-07-2001||10:54 PM||||Thank You for the info guys... I ordered them today...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||14
